-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ATTRIBUTION CARVE-OUT
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Filled-in disclosure forms are yours. You do NOT need to attribute this
repository when publishing a completed disclosure form alongside your own
results.

Attribution is asked for when you reproduce or adapt the SPECIFICATION itself --
the field definitions, the taxonomy, or the schema.

If you wish to attribute anyway, one line suffices:

    Contamination Disclosure v1 - CC BY 4.0

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NOTE FOR THE REPOSITORY MAINTAINER
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

GitHub will not display a licence badge or populate the repository's licence
field from this stub. Before or shortly after making the repository public, use
GitHub's licence picker (Add file -> Create new file -> type "LICENSE" ->
"Choose a license template" -> "Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International")
to insert the full CC BY 4.0 legal code, then re-append the ATTRIBUTION CARVE-OUT
section above to the end of the file. Delete this note once done.
